### Runnable from the IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client against `./mvnw spring-boot:run`.
### Sign-in uses the authorization code flow with PKCE (configured in http-client.env.json): the first request
### that needs a token opens Keycloak's login page. Demo accounts are listed in the README.
@host = http://localhost:8080

### Browse the demo catalogue (no sign-in needed)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products

### Add a product with only three units. Sign in as mira@flash-sale.local (catalog-manager).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{$auth.token("catalog-manager")}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "DROP-001",
  "name": "Limited sneaker",
  "price": 1499.90,
  "initialStock": 3
}

### Place an order. Sign in as alice@flash-sale.local (customer). Send it twice: the second response is 200 with the same order.
# @name placeOrder
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{$auth.token("customer")}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: checkout-001

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": 1, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Pay within the reservation window
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}/payment
Authorization: Bearer {{$auth.token("customer")}}

### ...or cancel and return the stock
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}/cancellation
Authorization: Bearer {{$auth.token("customer")}}

### Look at the order
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{$auth.token("customer")}}

### Without a token: 401, and the challenge points at the metadata below
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.id}}

### Where to get a token (RFC 9728)
GET {{host}}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource
